  "text_md": "## (12) United States Patent Uchiyama et al.\n\n## (54) STABLE, AQUEOUS COMPOSITIONS FOR TREATING SURFACES, ESPECIALLY FABRICS\n\n- 75) Inventors:\n\nHirotaka Uchiyama, Symmes OH (US); Janese Christine OBrien Stickney, Wyoming, OH (US); Jonathan Robert Cetti, Fairfield, OH (US); Ricky Ah-Man Woo, Hamilton, OH (US); Dean Larry DuVal, Lebanon; OH (US); Gayle Marie Frankenbach, Cincinnati, OH (US) Twp,\n\n- (73) Assignee:\n\nThe Procter &amp; Gamble Company, Cincinnati, OH (US)\n\n- Notice:\n\nSubject to any disclaimer; the term of this patent is extended Or adjusted under 35 US.C. 154(b) by 0 days.\n\n- (21) Appl. No.\n\n09/783,509\n\n- (22) Filed:\n\nFeb. 14, 2001\n\n- (65) Prior Publication Data\n\nUS 2002/0011584 Al Jan. 31, 2002\n\n## Related U.S. Application Data\n\n- (63) Continuation-in-part of application No. 09/634,379 filed on 9, 2000. Aug;\n- (60) Provisional application No: 60/240,626, filed on Oct. 16, 200O, and provisional application No. 60/182,381, filed on Feb. 2000. 14,\n\n- (51) Int. CI.\n\nDO6M 15/643\n\n- (52) 252/8.91; 252/8.61; 424/76.1; 424/76.2\n\n- 58) Field of Search 252/8.61, 8 424/76.1, 76.2 91;\n\n## 56) References Cited\n\n## U.S. PATENT DOCUMENTS\n\n|   3,299,112 | 1/1967   Bailey   |                             | 516/199   |\n|-------------|-------------------|-----------------------------|-----------|\n|   3,359,212 | 12/1967   Bailey  |                             |           |\n|   3,526,651 |                   | 9/1970   Rossmy et al.      | 556/446   |\n|   4,005,024 | 1/1977            | Rodriguez et al.            |           |\n|   4,661,268 | 4/1987            | Jacobson et al.             |           |\n|   5,482,703 | 1/1996            | Pings                       | 424/70.12 |\n|   5,500,254 |                   | 3/1996   Quincy; III et al. |           |\n|   5,525,415 | 6/1996            |                             |           |\n|   5,540,984 |                   | 7/1996   Quincy; III et al. |           |\n|   5,654,262 | 8/1997            | Desai et al.                | 510/112   |\n|   5,741,760 | 4/1998            | Mondin et al.               | 510/101   |\n|   5,804,625 | 9/1998            | Temperante                  |           |\n|   5,858,335 | 1/1999            | Lucas et al.                | 422/5     |\n|   5,861,147 | 1/1999            | Dodd et al.                 | 422/5     |\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nUS006503413B2\n\n- (10) Patent No::\n\nUS 6,503,413 B2\n\n- (45) Date of Patent:\n\nJan. 7,2003\n\n|   5,942,217 |    | 8/1999   | Woo et al.            |\n|-------------|----|----------|-----------------------|\n|   5,955,093 |    | 9/1999   | Woo et al.            |\n|   5,968,404 |    | 10/1999  | Trinh et al.          |\n|   5,968,990 |    | 10/1999  | Jon et al             |\n|   5,997,759 |    | 12/1999  | Trinh et al.          |\n|   6,001,343 |    | 12/1999  | Trinh et al.          |\n|   6,033,679 |    | 3/2000   | Woo et al.            |\n|   6,077,317 |    | 6/2000   | Murphy                |\n|   6,100,233 |    | 8/2000   | Sivik et al.          |\n|   6,106,738 |    | 8/2000   | Woo et al. 106/205.01 |\n|   6,284,231 | BI | 9/2001   | Trinh et al. 424/76.1 |\n\n## FOREIGN PATENT DOCUMENTS\n\n| GB   | 805768        | 12/1958 4/1995   |\n|------|---------------|------------------|\n| JP   | 7109486       |                  |\n| WO   | WO 9807455 Al | 2/1998           |\n| WO   | WO 9856429 Al | 12/1998          |\n| WO   | WO 9856888 Al | 12/1998          |\n| WO   | WO 9856890 Al | 12/1998          |\n| WO   | WO 9910767 Al | 3/1999           |\n| WO   | WO 9933669 Al | 7/1999           |\n| WO   | WO 9955814 Al | 11/1999          |\n| WO   | WO 9955815 Al | 11/1999          |\n| WO   | WO 9955948 Al | 11/1999          |\n| WO   | WO 9955949 Al | 11/1999          |\n| WO   | WO 9955950 Al | 11/1999          |\n| WO   | WO 9955951 Al | 11/1999          |\n| WO   | WO 9955952 Al | 11/1999          |\n| WO   | WO 9955953 Al | 11/1999          |\n| WO   | WO 0008249 Al | 2/2000           |\n| WO   | WO 0024851 A2 | 5/2000           |\n| WO   | WO 0024856 Al | 5/2000           |\n| WO   | WO 0024858 Al | 5/2000           |\n| WO   | WO 0030691 Al | 6/2000           |\n| WO   | WO 0055292 Al | 9/2000           |\n\nPrimary Examiner\\_ Anthony J. (74) Attorney; Agent; or Firm\\_Jeffrey V. Bamber; Jason J . Camp Green\n\n## (57) ABSTRACT\n\nStable, aqueous  compositions treating  surfaces, especially fabrics; comprise: relatively low molecular weight polyalkyleneoxide polysiloxane surfactant; buffering agent to maintain the pH of the composition in the range of from about 4 to about 10, preferably from about 5 to about 9.5, and more preferably from about 6 to about 9; and an aqueous carrier. The   compositions can further   comprise   catoinic surfactants to further enhance the spreading andlor fabric penetration ability of the compositions. The compositions can further comprise variety of other optional ingredients. Methods of treating surfaces include methods wherein the compositions are contacted with surfaces; especially fabrics, to reduce malodor impression on the surfaces andfor reduce the appearance of wrinkles in fabrics. for\n\n29 Claims, No Drawings",
